Clinical Course: The hospital team will closely monitor his brain activity and likely administer a continuous intravenous drip of anti-seizure medication to ensure the convulsions do not return.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

(To Spouse): Keep him exactly as he is, on his side. Do not put anything in his mouth. We are manually keeping his airway open while the medication allows his brain to reset.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: I have given him a massive dose of a muscle relaxant and anti-seizure drug to force his brain's electrical system to reboot. The seizure has stopped, but his brain is completely exhausted, which is why he is in a deep coma right now.
Actionable Steps: Let the paramedics take over his airway management as soon as they arrive. Please gather his empty medication bottles so the doctors know exactly what he has missed over the last few days.

